  "author": {
    "fr-FR": "Sainte Thérèse de l’Enfant-Jésus",
    "en-US": "St. Thérèse of Lisieux",
    "pt-BR": "Santa Teresinha do Menino Jesus"
  },
  "description": {
    "en-US": "The English verse translation of Thérèse’s poems by S. L. Emery (Angel Guardian Press, Boston, 1907), made from the 1898 texts as Mother Agnes retouched them: thirty-seven poems and plays in five parts, from “My Song of To-Day” and “To Live of Love” to “Why I Love Thee, Mary”, the Christmas and Egypt plays, and the Joan of Arc plays. It does not follow the numbering of the authentic Centenary poems, so it stands as a separate book beside them.",
    "fr-FR": "La traduction anglaise en vers des poésies de Thérèse par S. L. Emery (Angel Guardian Press, Boston, 1907), faite d’après les textes de 1898 retouchés par Mère Agnès : trente-sept poèmes et pièces en cinq parties. Elle ne suit pas la numérotation des poésies authentiques de l’édition du Centenaire ; c’est donc un livre distinct.",
    "pt-BR": "A tradução inglesa em verso dos poemas de Teresinha por S. L. Emery (Angel Guardian Press, Boston, 1907), feita a partir dos textos de 1898 retocados por Madre Inês: trinta e sete poemas e peças em cinco partes. Não segue a numeração dos poemas autênticos da edição do Centenário e por isso é um livro à parte."
  },
  "composed": "1893–1897",
  "languages": [
    "en-US"
  ],
  "work": "therese-of-lisieux/poems-emery",
  "editions": {
    "en-US": {
      "translator": "S. L. Emery",
      "year": 1907
    }
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "language": "en-US",
      "url": "https://ccel.org/ccel/t/therese/poems.xml",
      "edition": "S. L. Emery (tr.), Poems of St. Teresa, Carmelite of Lisieux, known as the Little Flower of Jesus, Boston: Angel Guardian Press, 1907; Christian Classics Ethereal Library ThML edition (ccel.org/ccel/therese/poems.html), verse structure as marked up there.",
      "description": "The poems and plays of the five parts, one chapter each. Left out: the translator's title page, dedication, contents, the index of dates, her introduction and the scripture index. The Scripture references printed under epigraphs are kept in italics. Speaker names in the plays are headings.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Published in Boston in 1907; S. L. Emery's death date is unknown to this project, but a 1907 American publication is public domain in the US."
    }
  ],
